  "comment": "The typed tracker result proposal a triage run submits (ADR 0277 decision 4, #5585 decision 5). A valid case gives the proposal and proposal_sha256, the SHA-256 of the canonical JSON (keys sorted, UTF-8, separators , and :, no insignificant whitespace) of the proposal with null members dropped. An invalid case gives the proposal and the expected issues as [field, code] pairs in any order; field is the dotted path, \"\" for the top level. A case with fill sets the text at path to char repeated length times before parsing, so oversized inputs stay small here. Read by apps/api/tests/test_factory_tracker_results.py; the runner result tool of #5586 reads it later. Readers reject unknown top-level keys.",
